  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Geo Group's total obligations are $894M for FY2026 to date. Geo Group has 113 awards so far, with an average award size of $7.9M, and obligations are up 13.0% year over year. Geo Group received the bulk of federal spending from two agencies. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $749M and the Department of Justice obligated $145M. Geo Group's principal markets are Security Guards and Patrol Services at $578M, Facilities Support Services at $189M, Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities at $81M, and Correctional Institutions at $46.3M. Historical obligations show a steady rise from FY23 through FY26: FY23 was $604M, FY24 was $642M, FY25 was $791M, and FY26 is $894M. This profile reflects concentration in a few markets and buyers, and a year-over-year increase in obligations, with current-year totals partial because figures are fiscal year to date. Contractors and subcontractors looking to work with Geo Group should note the firm’s large DHS relationship and the dominance of security and facilities support work in its federal portfolio.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Geo Group's biggest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is Geo Group's largest federal buyer at $749M. The Department of Justice is the second-largest buyer at $145M. Those two agencies together account for the majority of Geo Group's FY2026 to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Geo Group's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is Geo Group's largest market at $578M. Facilities Support Services is the next-largest market at $189M, followed by Other Justice, Public Order, and Safety Activities at $81M and Correctional Institutions at $46.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
